      "title": "Rational nondegeneracy does not guarantee an integral Betti adjoint",
      "statement": "Integral adjunction is P_H S=Q^T P_G. It exists iff the right-hand columns lie in the integral column lattice of P_H. A zero radical gives uniqueness, but a torsion cokernel can still prevent existence.",
